From: AROS eza port maintainers
Date: 2026-10-21
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: gate styles, icons and OSC 8 links on console capabilities
Repository: eza
Base-Commit: 98442ab17c2c3738701b62a7e060b1431ae2d6ea
Preceding-Patches: 0001 0002 0003 0004
Upstream-Status: AROS-specific, not for upstream
Scope: target_os = "aros" only, except formatting of src/aros.rs and pure
helpers in src/aros_policy.rs that are unit tested on the host.

The candidate refused --icons and --hyperlink outright and passed every SGR
attribute through. Limpet's presentation query (SDK tty_control.h,
XTY_PRESENT_KNOWN_* and XTY_FEATURE_*) now reports which style resets,
OSC 8 and the eza Nerd Font repertoire with one-cell icons are available.
- Output drops SGR attributes whose style bit is not confirmed, keeps colour
  arguments, and passes OSC 8 only when XTY_FEATURE_OSC8 is confirmed;
  sequences split across writes are reassembled, oversized ones discarded.
- Icons are enabled only when both XTY_FEATURE_NERD_ICONS_EZA and
  XTY_FEATURE_ICON_WIDTH_ONE are set; otherwise the option is ignored.
- Hyperlinks use file:///VOLUME:path with every byte outside unreserved,
  "/" and ":" percent-encoded (spaces, "#", "?", "%", non-ASCII).
- filename() keeps names ending in "//" (parent references) whole, escaping
  invalid bytes in them as elsewhere.
- Cargo.lock: libgit2-sys 0.18.5+1.9.4 is supplied by a path patch carrying
  the AROS local-repository build (patches/deps), so source and checksum are
  omitted; the version stays pinned.

Verification: host tests in src/aros_policy.rs. Native behaviour is recorded
in the port's validation documents; host tests do not establish it.
Removal: none planned; adapt when the presentation contract changes.

